{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3277","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3277","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3277\",\"parent_revision\":\"471a908220f47c47eafb3b3414becf252e873a9894fadffdfdb760df024fbadc\",\"root_revision\":\"471a908220f47c47eafb3b3414becf252e873a9894fadffdfdb760df024fbadc\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-28\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nObserved 2026-08-28/29 while running `/dh:work-backlog-item work --auto #3268`: `dh:swarm-task-planner` produced plan Pb31107bf with a populated `acceptance-criteria-structured` list (6 entries, each with a `check-command`, `expected-baseline`, and `expected-final`), but generated no `T0` or `TN` bookend tasks.\\n\\n`implement-feature/SKILL.md`'s \\\"Bookend Task Ordering\\\" section states this is not optional: \\\"When the plan contains `acceptance-criteria-structured` entries, `swarm-task-planner` generates T0 and TN bookend tasks. No special handling is needed in this loop \u2014 existing readiness logic dispatches them in the correct order automatically.\\\" T0 (`t0-baseline-capture`, `priority: 1`, `dependencies: []`) is meant to be the first ready task, capturing real command output before any implementation edit lands. TN (`tn-verification-gate`, `dependencies: [all non-bookend task IDs]`) is meant to run last, re-running the same commands and registering a `TN-verification` artifact for `/dh:complete-implementation`'s Pre-Phase-1 check.\\n\\nPlan Pb31107bf's task list is T1, T2, T3, T4, T5, T6 only \u2014 no T0, no TN \u2014 despite carrying a fully-formed `acceptance-criteria-structured` array that is exactly the input the Bookend Task Ordering contract says triggers their generation.\\n\\n**Consequence, verified by reading `complete-implementation/SKILL.md`'s Pre-Phase 1 TN Verification Check**: when the `TN-verification` artifact is absent, the check treats it as \\\"No structured criteria \u2014 proceed to Phase 1\\\" and silently skips verification entirely. This is indistinguishable, from the gate's perspective, from a plan that genuinely has no structured acceptance criteria to verify \u2014 it does not distinguish \\\"nothing to check\\\" from \\\"something to check that was never captured.\\\" The plan's 6 structured criteria therefore never get an independent, empirically-measured before/after comparison: each implementation task's own verification-steps duplicate the equivalent grep check, but those are self-reported by the same agent that made the edit, not an independent T0 baseline measured before any edit landed, and no single TN pass re-runs all 6 checks together after everything completes to catch cross-task regressions.\\n\\nUser-provided context: none \u2014 the fix (why `swarm-task-planner` skipped bookend generation for this input) has not been investigated; this item captures the observed defect and its verified downstream consequence, not a diagnosed root cause.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 development-harness /dh:work-backlog-item work --auto #3268, plan Pb31107bf\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-28\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"ad03f18b1620cff5898a11b615c52f2df322b166c1225997517a492192ef1b50\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABRRdG3Q\"}"}